<TeXmacs|2.1.5>

<style|book>

<\body>
  <doc-data|<doc-title|A short book>>

  <\table-of-contents|toc>
  </table-of-contents>

  <chapter|First chapter>

  A book is divided into chapters, which start on a new page and carry the
  running headers. This paragraph is the first one of the first chapter.

  <section|A section of the first chapter>

  Sections are numbered within their chapter.

  <\big-figure|<tabular|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-tborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<table|<row|<cell|figure
  content>>>>>>
    A figure, numbered within the chapter.
  </big-figure>

  <new-page>

  This paragraph starts on a page of its own, after an explicit page break.

  <chapter|Second chapter>

  <section|Another section>

  The second chapter is numbered two, and its first section 2.1.

  <\theorem>
    A theorem in a book is numbered within its chapter.
  </theorem>

  <appendix|An appendix>

  Appendices are numbered with letters.
</body>

<initial|<\collection>
<associate|page-medium|paper>
</collection>>
